00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:36.080
Let's decide on a place to stay overnight and rest early today.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:40.680
I used to have a night out in the woods around here.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.810
I had it, I had it.

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.270
I was trying to make pork soup and I got a burn.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:47.260
Soup?

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:48.630
Are you hungry?

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:52.710
If you want some of the rest of your lunch, I'll give you some.

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:53.950
I don't need it.

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:54.820
I see.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:56.860
Let's go buy something we can use for dinner.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:58.860
Ah...

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:01.980
What do you want to eat, Marshal?

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:05.650
If I have hope, I'll try as hard as I can.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.680
Even if you say that...

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:11.700
But you're going to eat monsters, aren't you?

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:16.590
If you can eat anything you want...

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.460
What kind of monsters do you see around here?

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:21.640
Um...

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:24.390
Big bat, big mouse...

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.350
I definitely don't want that!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:27.930
Forest goblin...

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:29.150
The non-human type is a waste of time!

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.240
Metal armor.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:31.280
Metal?

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:33.620
Isn't there something more ordinary?

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.660
Like a bird or a tree.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.000
There is.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.120
This guy who doesn't care about anything but hates me.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.140
Am I that selfish?

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:46.370
There are ordinary things, but they don't attack.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.700
If you want to hunt, you have to be prepared.

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.000
There is no such thing as an ant eating green onions.

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:53.490
I'm sorry.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.420
That's right.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:55.340
However!

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.480
It may be possible that a monster turtle with a human-eating green onion will come out.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:58.960
It's a maze.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:17:59.440
Thank you very much!

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:00.900
Let's try to enjoy it!

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.220
I can't be that positive.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:07.930
No, there are a lot of trees and fruits in this season.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:17.640
It's a tree of plants!

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.120
Marcel, that's wrong.

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:23.720
Human-eating plants are called, for example, that flower.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.690
Its official name is Balacelia.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.570
It mainly lives on the animal road.

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:29.310
It's like a spider's thread.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.080
When you touch a plant, it will attract you.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:37.300
It will be attracted to the moving things but it has no digestive ability.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.020
It is a plant that produces its own metabolism.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.420
But it has the tendency to make people its food, doesn't it?

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:44.910
Usually you can eat it.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.420
The vegetables that the dead eat are also made from the feces and dead skin of the living.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.830
I don't think that's the right way to put it.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.140
It's okay. We're still on the second floor.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:58.920
If there's a corpse lying around here, someone will notice it.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:05.300
There is also a reunion party, and anyway, there is no one who can be a demon's bait in a place like this.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:07.560
Is that so?

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.630
It seems difficult to mow secretly.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:12.840
I have no choice but to fight.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.140
Get out of there!

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:19.460
I'll clean it up for you all.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:27.940
Sperae, Ieptum, Lephermus, Alamandras, Projus, Lixantra!

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:29.100
Stop it!

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:31.320
What? Why?

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.120
Are you going to blow it away with magic?

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:41.750
I'll take as much as I eat. This is the iron rule.

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.090
You're not going to do it!

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:46.580
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:58.460
Huh? No, there's someone with a fire extinguisher.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:05.890
It depends on the species. By the way, what Marcyl is holding right now is a parasitic type that plants seeds under the skin.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:18.960
Don't move too much, Marcyl. Plant-type monsters have many arms. If you fight them one by one, the sun will set. If you put your teeth in, just one place.

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:20.690
The root!

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:28.000
Are you okay?

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:29.880
Thank you.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.940
Torayo-san...

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:32.000
How was it?

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:32.810
Huh?

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:36.750
This is called the Shadow Tail, which grows seeds under the skin of a living creature.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.220
Compared to the Barselia species, which entwines their claws so strongly that they are fractured,

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:45.120
It is necessary to capture without missing or killing the target.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:49.890
I know the balance between not being able to move and not being able to feel uncomfortable.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:52.850
It's really...

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.770
I think it feels good, but...

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:55.550
How was it?

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:58.980
I made her angry again.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.780
I think I can do it, too.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:15.690
First, lightly steam it.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:22.440
Cut it along the edges, twist it a little, and pull it to remove the seeds.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:23.380
Oh!

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:29.520
Peel it, beat it well, soften it, and put it in a frying pan.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.700
Put the slime and a little bit of scorpion juice in the crumbled squid and mix it until it becomes sticky.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:42.880
When it becomes smooth, add the rest of the scorpion juice and chopped wood.

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:48.240
After mixing roughly, pour it into a frying pan and heat it for a while.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:50.680
I want to try if I can grow it on the ground!

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:52.560
Of course it's useless!

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:58.840
When the surface becomes rough, add the rest of the fruit.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.340
All right, it's done.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:10.480
It's just a show, but the skin doesn't burn.

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:11.740
You can leave it.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.700
It tastes like salt.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:14.920
It's different from what I imagined.

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:17.520
It's delicious.

00:22:17.780 --> 00:22:19.480
Try it, Marshal.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.320
It's probably your favorite flavor.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.530
I don't think there's a plant with a dead body in it.

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:26.870
I didn't put it in.

00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:29.060
If you use the gelatin that accumulates in that plant,

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.550
It's more beautiful, but the slime doesn't harden well.

00:22:41.550 --> 00:22:45.300
It's fresh and sweet.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:46.580
It has a strong taste of digested.

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:49.620
But is that okay?

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:53.320
If it's delicious, it's a feast for other animals, isn't it?

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:55.520
Even if I eat it, I'll be eaten.

00:22:56.420 --> 00:22:58.460
Because it's a carnivorous plant.

00:22:58.460 --> 00:22:58.820
Because it's a monster.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.780
I'll take the animal and turn it into a nutrient.

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:03.200
Oh, I see.

00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:06.480
Well, then, is this deliciousness also a strategy?

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:08.250
I see.

00:23:09.960 --> 00:23:13.590
I'm glad you're starting to be interested.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:15.500
Stop it!

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:25.260
So, what about that corpse?

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:27.810
It's impossible to go back to the town now.

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:28.130
I can't do it.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.760
Let's make him come back to life.

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:34.030
Let's stop it. There's a chance we'll fail.

00:23:35.070 --> 00:23:38.210
If we leave it where it looks good, someone will pick it up.

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:42.230
That's right. So that it stands out as much as possible.

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:46.160
I've seen something like this at the execution ground.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:53.420
